Create a read-only Claude Agent SDK inspection session. Deny Write and Edit before any modification, without prompting the user.

```python
from claude_agent_sdk import ClaudeAgentOptions, HookMatcher

async def deny_writes(input_data, tool_use_id, context):
    return {
        "hookSpecificOutput": {
            "hookEventName": input_data["hook_event_name"],
            "permissionDecision": [B],
            "permissionDecisionReason": "This is a read-only session",
        }
    }

options = ClaudeAgentOptions(
    hooks={[A]: [HookMatcher(matcher="Write|Edit", hooks=[deny_writes])]}
)
```

Which values correctly fill [A] and [B]?

Create a Google ADK order-query agent. In read-only mode, block update_order and cancel_order but permit all other tools. The callback runs immediately before execution.

```python
from google.adk.agents import LlmAgent

WRITE_TOOLS = {"update_order", "cancel_order"}

def guard(tool, args, tool_context):
    if tool.name in WRITE_TOOLS:
        return {"error": "Writes are not allowed in read-only mode."}
    return [B]

agent = LlmAgent(
    name="orders", model="gemini-flash-latest",
    tools=[get_order, update_order, cancel_order],
    [A]=guard,
)
```

Which values correctly fill [A] and [B]?
